IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-worker`
IMPORT `whs-regulations`

-- Work Health and Safety Regulations 2011 -- worked cases, from the worker's seat. Expected values were written by hand from
-- the deposited Regulations (Compilation No. 28) and the Act, never copied from the encoding's output. All facts are
-- HYPOTHETICAL.

-- reg 699. A nurse at a Defence health centre catches an infection from a patient: notifiable though no hospital admission.
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `another injury, illness or incident` `an infection to which my work was a significant contributing factor` TRUE
-- A meat inspector at a Commonwealth export abattoir contracts Q fever: notifiable.
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `another injury, illness or incident` `Q fever, anthrax, leptospirosis, brucellosis, Hendra virus, avian influenza or psittacosis, caught in work with animals or animal products` TRUE
-- A cold caught at the office: not notifiable.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `another injury, illness or incident` `another illness, or none` TRUE
-- A hospital admission is notifiable under the Act alone; the illness question changes nothing.
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `someone needed immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient` `another illness, or none` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `someone needed immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient` `an infection to which my work was a significant contributing factor` TRUE
-- Q fever caught by a visitor that did not arise out of the business's work: not notifiable by it.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a notifiable incident under the Regulations` `another injury, illness or incident` `Q fever, anthrax, leptospirosis, brucellosis, Hendra virus, avian influenza or psittacosis, caught in work with animals or animal products` FALSE
-- Mirror on the Act's own module: the same Q fever case with the regulations input set by hand.
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident` `another injury, illness or incident` TRUE TRUE

-- regs 22, 23.
#ASSERT `What procedure resolves my safety issue` FALSE EQUALS `I may start it by telling the business (and any other party) that there is an issue and its nature and scope; all parties must then meet or communicate to try to resolve it, having regard to the risk, who is affected, the measures needed and who will carry them out; I may be assisted or represented by a person I nominate (reg 23(2)-(5))`
#ASSERT `What procedure resolves my safety issue` TRUE EQUALS `the agreed procedure applies, and it must include the default procedure's steps, be in writing and have been communicated to me (reg 22)`
#ASSERT `Must the resolution be written and given to me` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the resolution be written and given to me` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must the resolution be written and given to me` FALSE TRUE

-- The default procedure as a rule. I raise the issue; the business meets with me: fulfilled.
#TRACE `the default procedure, started by me` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `I, the worker (or my representative)` DOES `tell each other party there is an issue, and its nature and scope` AT 1
    PARTY `the business or undertaking` DOES `meet or communicate to attempt to resolve the issue` AT 2
-- A written agreement was asked for; the business writes it and gives copies: fulfilled.
#TRACE `the written agreement, when I ask for it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the business or undertaking` DOES `set out the issue and its resolution in a written agreement` AT 1
    PARTY `the business or undertaking` DOES `give each party a copy of the written agreement` AT 2

-- reg 24. A worker stopped work near an unguarded live conductor and did the safe alternative work offered: long service
-- leave keeps its continuity.
#ASSERT `Is my continuity kept for this entitlement` `my leave entitlements` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `protected: ceasing the unsafe work does not break my continuity of engagement for working out this entitlement (s 88, reg 24)`
#ASSERT `Is my continuity kept for this entitlement` `my superannuation benefits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `protected: ceasing the unsafe work does not break my continuity of engagement for working out this entitlement (s 88, reg 24)`
#ASSERT `Is my continuity kept for this entitlement` `my entitlement to notice of termination` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not protected: I unreasonably failed to do safe and appropriate alternative work I was directed to do (s 88)`

-- reg 12A.
#ASSERT `Is my licensee's transitional period running` `MLC Wealth Limited` (Date 1 6 2022) EQUALS `running: the Act applies to my work for it (s 12(4), (6))`
#ASSERT `Is my licensee's transitional period running` `Vicinity Centres PM Pty Ltd` (Date 23 10 2026) EQUALS `ended: the day reg 12A prescribes has passed, so the Act no longer applies to my work for it by s 12(4)`
#ASSERT `Is my licensee's transitional period running` `Hollard Insurance Partners Limited` (Date 1 4 2023) EQUALS `ended: the day reg 12A prescribes has passed, so the Act no longer applies to my work for it by s 12(4)`
#ASSERT `Is my licensee's transitional period running` `Hollard Insurance Partners Limited` (Date 1 2 2023) EQUALS `not known from the deposit: the period ended on 4 January 2023 or 1 April 2023, and the Regulations' endnotes do not say which`
#ASSERT `Is my licensee's transitional period running` `another non-Commonwealth licensee` (Date 23 10 2026) EQUALS `running: the Act applies to my work for it (s 12(4), (6))`
